      {
        "id": 262218,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-01-28T19:35:07.055Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"der_andere_Jan\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"31304\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/48/1881_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> der_andere_Jan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But if you don’t mind someone reading along, could you post a link so that I can get an impression of how pbp works over there?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The site does open campaigns (unlike some that keep everything hidden except to participants) so that’s no problem, but the GM volunteer is refreshing themselves on the rules and hasn’t started up the recruitment/session zero thread yet.  I’ll pass it along when it goes live.</p>\n<p>FWIW, here’s links to two recently-defunct Sentinels PbP games over on the same site if you want to see two different styles of running the game.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/sentinel-comics-crackerjacks.912073/\">Crackerjacks IC</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/sentinel-comics-crackerjacks.912074/\">Crackerjacks OOC</a></p>\n<p>According to the GM this one just kind of petered out, which is a shame.  I was curious to see where the plot was going just from reading along, and it featured some nice tight action scenes.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/sentinel-comics-the-pivotal-point-guard.916361/\">Pivotal Point Guard IC</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/sentinel-comics-the-pivotal-point-guard.916362/\">Pivotal Point Guard OOC</a></p>\n<p>FrivYeti and I joined the Pivotal Point Guard game partway through when they had some openings due to player attrition.  The GM just got a new position at work and between that and some personal stuff they felt they had to step back from the game.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-01-28T19:35:07.055Z",
